  SPAN LIMIT -- the last hop count that still decodes

      section  repeaters   total span
           1k         24        25.0k
         1.5k          3         6.0k
           2k          1         4.0k

  "locked" is the fraction of the clip the framer held, and BER is
  scored INSIDE that -- so read the two together: a high BER with a
  low locked% is a chain that broke, and so is a low BER with one.
  The span limit below requires locked > 95% as well as BER = 0.

  Edges are matched to the nearest ideal edge within half a cell,
  after the chain's bulk delay -- one input filter a section -- is
  removed, because a constant delay is not distortion.  "stray" is
  an edge the chain invented and "lost" one it swallowed; either is
  what a biphase slip is made of.

  The displacement accumulates as a BIAS, not a random walk: each
  section's comparator fires a little late or a little early on the
  same side every time, and the next section re-launches that as a
  real edge.  So the lever is where the slicing level sits -- DC
  restore and threshold centring -- not gain, and not more sections.

